Hopefully, journalists don't write fiction, which was the subject at the ti=
me.=20
 They are more likely to use evidentials than counterfactuals.

But now, back to 101. =20
As Mad Ludwig used to say, there are a number of language games, only a ver=
y few=20
of which are about stating facts. Y'all seem to be trying to reduce a large=
=20
number of other games to these few.  Lojban (thx Loglan) makes quite explic=
it=20
devices for playing at a number of others.  Some of these are reasonably=20
familiar (or, at least, parts of them are): There is the impelling -others =
game=20
of imperatives and hortatives (Go!, Let's go).  There is the moral=20
world-changing game of promises and vows.  There is the rather related game=
 of=20
expressing ones intentions (not quite a vow or promise, but similar enough =
to be=20
dealt with in a similar way).  There is the meaning-world creation of=20
counterfactuals, which is very different from any of these, since it takes =
one=20
out of the present context and puts one in another altogether -- but not in=
 a=20
story-telling sort of way.  And there are many more.
To say that 'ai mi bedgo' (Panlan, a literary shadow of early Loglan) means=
 "It=20
is my intention to go to bed", which might be either true or false, dependi=
ng on=20
my state of mind, is just to think the speaker is playing chess when he is=
=20
really playing Bridge.  "I'm gonta bed" is better; it is more clearly merel=
y an=20
expression of intention.  The response "Oh no you aren't " is not a declara=
tion=20
that some claim the sentence made (it didn't make one) is false but either=
=20
introduces a (presumed dominant) intension: "You're gonna finish washing th=
e=20
dishes" or a question of sincerity ("I know you are really planning on snea=
king=20
off to snog with your boyfriend"). =20
You get some fun when you try to report these utterances with other than di=
rect=20
quotes:  "She said that she was going to bed" probably works in English bec=
ause=20
of the unlikelihood of this being a prediction, but doing the same in Lojba=
n=20
might raise problems.  I admit I no longer remember what to do in these cas=
es=20
nor whether the issue was ever raised or answered.  Have fun!


